{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
I [G]dream of Jeanie with the [C]light brown [G]hair,
[G]Borne, like a [Em]vapor, on the [A7]summer [D7]air;
I [G]see her tripping
Where the [C]bright streams [G]play,
[G]Happy as the [Am]daisies
That [D7]dance on her [G]way.
[C]Many were the [G]wild notes
Her [Am]merry voice would [D7]pour,
[C]Many were the [G]blithe birds
That [A7]warbled them [D7]o'er:
Oh! I [G]dream of Jeanie with the [C]light brown [G]hair,
[G]Floating, like a [Am]vapor,
On the [D7]soft summer [G]air.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
I [G]long for Jeanie with the [C]daydawn [G]smile,
[G]Radiant in [Em]gladness, warm with [A7]winning [D7]guile;
I [G]hear her melodies,
[C]Like joys gone [G]by,
[G]Sighing round my [Am]heart
O'er the [D7]fond hopes that [G]die:
[C]Sighing like the [G]night wind
And [Am]sobbing like the [D7]rain,
[C]Wailing for the [G]lost one
That [A7]comes not a[D7]gain:
Oh! I [G]long for Jeanie, and my [C]heart bows [G]low,
[G]Never more to [Am]find her
Where the [D7]bright waters [G]flow.
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: G}
